<HelpChapterSection Id="documents">
    <HelpTopicSection Id="documents-list">
        <p>Open <span class="help-ui">Documents</span> in the menu. This is the registry of all documents you have access to.</p>
        <h4>Tabs</h4>
        <ul>
            <li><span class="help-ui">Awaiting my signature</span> — opens by default: documents where it is <strong>your turn</strong> to sign.</li>
            <li><span class="help-ui">Created by me</span> — documents you are the author of.</li>
            <li><span class="help-ui">I'm in the route</span> — documents where you are a signer (whether or not you have already signed).</li>
            <li><span class="help-ui">Signed by me</span> — documents you have already signed. Open a document card from here to download the file together with its signatures.</li>
            <li><span class="help-ui">All available</span> — all documents you are allowed to see (see “<a href="/help#documents-visibility">Whose documents you see</a>”).</li>
        </ul>
        <h4>Search and filters</h4>
        <ul>
            <li>Search box — by title or registration number; click <span class="help-ui">Search</span> or press Enter.</li>
            <li>Status filter — <span class="help-ui">All statuses</span> or one of the statuses: “Draft”, “In signing”, “Signed”, “Rejected”, “Archived”.</li>
            <li>Type filter — <span class="help-ui">All types</span> or: “Order”, “Directive”, “Memo”, “Application”, “Report”, “Minutes”, “Contract”, “Certificate”, “Regulation / instruction”, “Letter”, “Act”, “Other document”.</li>
            <li>Filters are applied as soon as you select them.</li>
        </ul>
        <h4>Table columns</h4>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Document</strong> — the title, with the type and unit below it.</li>
            <li><strong>Number</strong> — the registration number.</li>
            <li><strong>Status</strong> — plus the <span class="help-ui">Your signature</span> badge if it's your turn now.</li>
            <li><strong>Signatures</strong> — how many of the required signatures have been applied (for example, 2/3).</li>
            <li><strong>Author</strong>, <strong>Created</strong>.</li>
            <li><strong>Actions</strong> — <span class="help-ui">Sign</span> if it's your turn, otherwise <span class="help-ui">Open</span>.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Sort by clicking the “Document”, “Number”, “Status” and “Created” headers (clicking again reverses the order). By default, the newest documents are at the top. If nothing is found, you'll see “No documents found” with a suggestion to change the search or filters.</p>
    </HelpTopicSection>

    <HelpTopicSection Id="documents-lifecycle">
        <div class="help-table-wrap">
            <table class="help-table">
                <thead><tr><th>Status</th><th>What it means</th><th>What's next</th></tr></thead>
                <tbody>
                    <tr><td>Draft</td><td>The document has been created but not sent for signing.</td><td>The author edits it, sends it for signing or deletes it.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>In signing</td><td>The document is going through the signing route.</td><td>Signers sign or decline. While there are no signatures yet, the author can withdraw the document back to drafts. A document in signing cannot be edited.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>Signed</td><td>All signers have signed. The “Completed” date is filled in.</td><td>The document can no longer change. It can only be archived.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>Rejected</td><td>One of the signers declined and gave a reason. The route is stopped.</td><td>The author corrects the document (edits the file, details or route) and sends it again, or archives it. It can be deleted if it has no signatures.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>Archived</td><td>The final state for completed documents.</td><td>A document cannot be restored from the archive.</td></tr>
                </tbody>
            </table>
        </div>
        <p>Signer statuses in the route: “Awaiting signature”, “Signed”, “Declined”.</p>
        <p>Each document automatically gets a <strong>registration number</strong> in the <code class="ds-code">YYYY/NNNNNN</code> format, for example <code class="ds-code">2026/000123</code>.</p>
        <Alert Tone="Tone.Outline" Icon="info" Title="When a document can be changed">The author can edit a document while it is “Draft” or “Rejected”. A document that is in signing, signed or archived cannot be changed — all signers sign the same file. For details, see “<a href="/help#documents-edit">Editing a draft or rejected document</a>”.</Alert>
    </HelpTopicSection>

    <HelpTopicSection Id="documents-create">
        <p>Click <span class="help-ui">New document</span> in the registry or on the home page. The page has three cards.</p>
        <h4>File</h4>
        <ol class="help-steps">
            <li>Drag a file into the <span class="help-ui">Drag a file here or click to select</span> area, or click it.</li>
            <li>Allowed types: PDF, DOC, DOCX, XLS, XLSX, PPT, PPTX, ODT, ODS, RTF, TXT, XML, JPG, JPEG, PNG, ZIP; size — up to <strong>25 MB</strong>. If the document will be signed in PAdES format (signature inside the PDF), upload a PDF.</li>
            <li>If you haven't entered a title yet, it is filled in from the file name.</li>
        </ol>
        <h4>Details</h4>
        <ul>
            <li><span class="help-ui">Title</span> (required, up to 300 characters), for example “On approval of the vacation schedule”.</li>
            <li><span class="help-ui">Document type</span> (required), “Memo” by default.</li>
            <li><span class="help-ui">Unit</span> (required) — the unit on whose behalf the document is issued. The list contains the units of your positions and the units nested in them; with the “Organization documents” permission — all units of your organizations; with the “All documents” permission — all units of the cabinet. If there is only one such unit, it is selected automatically.</li>
            <li><span class="help-ui">Description</span> (up to 4000 characters) — a short summary or a comment for the signers.</li>
        </ul>
        <h4>Signing route</h4>
        <p>Add signers — see “<a href="/help#documents-route">Signing route</a>”.</p>
        <h4>Saving</h4>
        <ul>
            <li><span class="help-ui">Create and send for signing</span> — the document immediately gets the “In signing” status, and it becomes the first signers' turn. The button is enabled only when at least one signer has been added. Message: “Document created and sent for signing”.</li>
            <li><span class="help-ui">Save draft</span> — the document is saved with the “Draft” status; you can send it later from its page. Message: “Draft saved”.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>After saving, the document page opens.</p>
        <h4>Possible errors</h4>
        <ul>
            <li>“Select the document file.”, “This file type is not supported.”, “The file size cannot exceed 25 MB.”</li>
            <li>“Enter the document title.”, “Select a unit.”, “Select a unit you belong to.”</li>
            <li>“Some signers are inactive or don't exist.” — one of the signers has been blocked; remove them from the route.</li>
        </ul>
    </HelpTopicSection>

    <HelpTopicSection Id="documents-route">
        <ol class="help-steps">
            <li>Choose the signing order: <span class="help-ui">Sequential</span> (one after another, the default) or <span class="help-ui">Parallel</span> (in any order).</li>
            <li>In the <span class="help-ui">Find an employee</span> box, start typing a last name, first name or email (at least 2 characters). Up to 10 active employees with their primary positions appear.</li>
            <li>Click an employee — they are added to the end of the route with a sequence number.</li>
            <li>Change the order with the <span class="help-ui">Up</span> and <span class="help-ui">Down</span> buttons, remove signers with <span class="help-ui">Remove</span>.</li>
        </ol>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Sequential:</strong> only the first signer in line who hasn't signed yet can sign. The next one sees the document under “Awaiting my signature” after the previous signer has signed. Suitable for bottom-up approval (specialist → head of division → director of department → head of organization).</li>
            <li><strong>Parallel:</strong> all signers can sign at the same time in any order. Suitable for documents signed by a committee.</li>
            <li>A maximum of 50 signers, each person only once.</li>
            <li>A document without signers can only be saved as a draft.</li>
        </ul>
    </HelpTopicSection>

    <HelpTopicSection Id="documents-card">
        <p>Open a document from the registry (its title or <span class="help-ui">Open</span>). At the top are the title, status, type and number, and on the right — the action buttons available to you right now.</p>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Document file</strong> — the file name, size and type, the <span class="help-ui">Download</span> button and the <strong>SHA-256</strong> line — the file's “fingerprint”, used to verify that the file hasn't been changed.</li>
            <li><strong>Details</strong> — registration number, type, unit (a link to its page), author, signing order, the “Created”, “Sent for signing” and “Completed” dates, and the description.</li>
            <li><strong>Signatures</strong> — all applied QES: the full name from the certificate; signature format, level and type; date; provider, certificate number, individual tax number / EDRPOU code; the <span class="help-ui">Download signature</span> button. If there are no signatures yet — “No signatures yet”.</li>
            <li><strong>Signing route</strong> — a timeline: step number, full name, position and unit, status and decision date. The reason for declining is highlighted in red.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>If it's your turn now, the hint “The document is awaiting your signature” appears at the top. The author of a draft or rejected document sees the <span class="help-ui">Edit</span> button, and for a rejected one also the “Document rejected” hint with advice on what to do next.</p>
        <p>If the document doesn't exist or you don't have access to it, you'll see “Document not found” with a <span class="help-ui">To registry</span> button.</p>
    </HelpTopicSection>

    <HelpTopicSection Id="documents-edit">
        <p>The author can change a document with the <strong>“Draft”</strong> or <strong>“Rejected”</strong> status — for example, to fix a mistake pointed out by a signer.</p>
        <ol class="help-steps">
            <li>Open the document and click <span class="help-ui">Edit</span>. The “Edit document” page opens with the current data.</li>
            <li>Replace the file if needed: in the “File” card, click <span class="help-ui">Replace file</span> and select a new one. The current file is shown above the selection area.</li>
            <li>Change the <span class="help-ui">Title</span>, <span class="help-ui">Document type</span>, <span class="help-ui">Unit</span> or <span class="help-ui">Description</span>.</li>
            <li>Change the route: the signing order, new signers, the sequence with the <span class="help-ui">Up</span> / <span class="help-ui">Down</span> buttons, unneeded signers with <span class="help-ui">Remove</span>.</li>
            <li>Click <span class="help-ui">Save changes</span> (the document keeps its current status) or <span class="help-ui">Save and send for signing</span>. <span class="help-ui">Cancel</span> returns to the document without changes.</li>
        </ol>
        <h4>What happens to signatures already applied</h4>
        <p>A rejected document may have signatures from those who signed before it was declined. When editing:</p>
        <div class="help-table-wrap">
            <table class="help-table">
                <thead><tr><th>What changed</th><th>Signatures</th></tr></thead>
                <tbody>
                    <tr><td>Title, type, unit, description, order of signers</td><td>Kept — these details are not part of the signed file.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>A signer was removed from the route</td><td>Their signature is deleted.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>The file was replaced</td><td><strong>All</strong> signatures are deleted: they were applied to the previous file. All signers will sign the new file.</td></tr>
                </tbody>
            </table>
        </div>
        <p>The editor warns you in advance: signers whose signatures will be kept are marked <span class="help-ui">Signature will be kept</span>, and if saving would delete signatures, a red warning with their count appears.</p>
        <p>The document's registration number doesn't change when it is edited. Every change is recorded in the audit log as “Document changed” (with the new file name and the number of revoked signatures).</p>
    </HelpTopicSection>

    <HelpTopicSection Id="documents-sign">
        <p>You can sign a document when it's your turn in the route and you have the “Sign documents” permission.</p>
        <ol class="help-steps">
            <li>Open the document (the <span class="help-ui">Awaiting my signature</span> tab or the <span class="help-ui">Sign</span> button in the registry) and review the file carefully — the <span class="help-ui">Download</span> button in the “Document file” card.</li>
            <li>Click <span class="help-ui">Sign</span> at the top of the page. The “Sign document” window opens with the number and file name.</li>
            <li><strong>The “Document” step.</strong> The browser downloads the file and compares its SHA-256 fingerprint with the registered one. If everything is fine — “Integrity confirmed”. If the fingerprint doesn't match — “The file checksum doesn't match the registered one. Signing is not allowed.” (contact your administrator). Click <span class="help-ui">Next</span>.</li>
            <li><strong>The “Parameters” step.</strong> Choose the format and level (CAdES, B-LT recommended; PAdES is available for PDF). Click <span class="help-ui">Next</span>.</li>
            <li><strong>The “Key and signature” step.</strong> Select the key file, enter the password, click <span class="help-ui">Read key</span>, check the owner's details and click <span class="help-ui">Sign</span>. More about keys — “<a href="/help#signing-keys">Keys and providers</a>”.</li>
            <li>“Document signed” appears — “Signature saved. The page will refresh automatically.” The signature appears in the “Signatures” card, and your step in the route becomes “Signed”.</li>
        </ol>
        <p>If you are the last signer, the document gets the “Signed” status. With sequential order, the next signer receives the document in their queue.</p>
        <p>Closing the signing window (the close button or a click outside the window) releases the key — the next time you open it, you'll need to read the key again.</p>
        <p>Possible errors: “The document is not awaiting your signature right now.” (it isn't your turn yet or the document has changed — refresh the page), “The PAdES format is available only for PDF documents.”, “The data was just changed by another user. Refresh the page and try again.”, as well as key errors (see “<a href="/help#signing-problems">Error messages</a>”).</p>
    </HelpTopicSection>

    <HelpTopicSection Id="documents-reject">
        <p>If the document contains a mistake or you disagree with it, decline to sign — the author will see the reason and can prepare a corrected document.</p>
        <ol class="help-steps">
            <li>Open the document and click <span class="help-ui">Decline</span>.</li>
            <li>In the “Decline signing” window, enter the <span class="help-ui">Reason</span> (required, up to 1000 characters) — specifically what needs to be fixed.</li>
            <li>Click <span class="help-ui">Decline</span>. “Decline recorded” appears.</li>
        </ol>
        <p>The very first decline stops the route: the document gets the “Rejected” status, and the other signers can no longer sign it. The reason is shown in red in the route. The author will correct the document and send it again — then it will reappear in your queue.</p>
    </HelpTopicSection>

    <HelpTopicSection Id="documents-author">
        <div class="help-table-wrap">
            <table class="help-table">
                <thead><tr><th>Button</th><th>When available</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead>
                <tbody>
                    <tr><td>Send for signing</td><td>The document is “Draft” or “Rejected” and has signers.</td><td>After confirming “Send the document for signing?”, the document gets the “In signing” status. Message: “Document sent for signing”.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>Withdraw</td><td>The document is “In signing” and nobody has signed it yet.</td><td>After confirming “Withdraw the document to drafts?”, the document returns to “Draft”. Message: “Document returned to drafts”.</td></tr>
                </tbody>
            </table>
        </div>
        <h4>Resending a rejected document</h4>
        <ol class="help-steps">
            <li>Read the reason for declining in the signing route.</li>
            <li>Correct the document with the <span class="help-ui">Edit</span> button (see “<a href="/help#documents-edit">Editing</a>”) and click <span class="help-ui">Save and send for signing</span>. If no corrections are needed, just click <span class="help-ui">Send for signing</span> on the document page.</li>
        </ol>
        <ul>
            <li>Those who have already signed the <strong>current file</strong> don't sign again: their signatures are kept, and their route step stays “Signed”.</li>
            <li>The other steps (including the one who declined) return to “Awaiting signature”; the reasons for declining are cleared.</li>
            <li>With sequential order, the first signer who hasn't signed yet becomes first in line.</li>
            <li>If after the changes all signers in the route have already signed the current file, the document immediately gets the “Signed” status.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Actions available only to the author show other users “Only the document author can perform this action.”</p>
    </HelpTopicSection>

    <HelpTopicSection Id="documents-files">
        <ul>
            <li><span class="help-ui">Download</span> in the “Document file” card — the original file.</li>
            <li><span class="help-ui">Download signature</span> in the “Signatures” card — the signature file. The file name consists of the document number (with “-” instead of “/”), the signer's full name and the format extension: <code class="ds-code">.p7s</code> (CAdES), <code class="ds-code">.xml</code> (XAdES), <code class="ds-code">.pdf</code> (PAdES), <code class="ds-code">.asics</code> / <code class="ds-code">.asice</code> (ASiC).</li>
            <li>To verify a signature, open <span class="help-ui">Signing</span> → <span class="help-ui">Verify</span> and add the signature file (for a detached signature, together with the original). See “<a href="/help#signing-verify">Verifying a signature</a>”.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Documents and signatures are stored on the server without public access and are served only to users who are allowed to see the document.</p>
    </HelpTopicSection>

    <HelpTopicSection Id="documents-archive">
        <div class="help-table-wrap">
            <table class="help-table">
                <thead><tr><th>Button</th><th>Who and when</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead>
                <tbody>
                    <tr><td>Archive</td><td>The author or a user with the “Manage documents” permission; the document is “Signed” or “Rejected”.</td><td>After confirming “Move the document to the archive?”, the status becomes “Archived”. A document cannot be restored from the archive. Message: “Document moved to the archive”.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><Icon Name="trash-2" /> (delete)</td><td>The author or “Manage documents”; the document has no signatures and isn't archived.</td><td>After confirming “Delete the document permanently?”, the document is deleted together with its file. Message: “Document deleted”.</td></tr>
                </tbody>
            </table>
        </div>
        <p>A document with signatures cannot be deleted — only archived: “A document with signatures can't be deleted — it can only be archived.”</p>
    </HelpTopicSection>

    <HelpTopicSection Id="documents-visibility">
        <ul>
            <li>You <strong>always</strong> see documents you are the author of and documents whose route you are in.</li>
            <li>With the <strong>“Unit documents”</strong> permission — also documents of the units of your positions and all nested units (for example, a department director sees the documents of the department and all its divisions and sections).</li>
            <li>With the <strong>“Organization documents”</strong> permission — documents of the entire organization where you hold a position, with all its units (head of organization, deputies, records clerks). Documents of other organizations in the cabinet are not visible.</li>
            <li>With the <strong>“All documents”</strong> permission — documents of all organizations in the cabinet (usually only for system administrators and auditors).</li>
        </ul>
        <p>A document you can't see is not shown in the registry, and a direct link to it shows “Document not found”.</p>
    </HelpTopicSection>
</HelpChapterSection>
